Fix efi_fuzz's build and Qiling API use

efi_fuzz was last touched in March 2021 and pins none of its dependencies.
Four upstream changes since then stop it working:

1. https://bootstrap.pypa.io/get-pip.py now requires Python 3.10+, but the
   Dockerfile is Ubuntu 20.04 (Python 3.8):

       ERROR: This script does not work on Python 3.8.

   pypa keeps per-version bootstrap scripts; use the 3.8 one.

2. uefi-firmware-parser's main branch moved to requires-python >=3.10:

       ERROR: Package 'uefi-firmware' requires a different Python:
       3.8.10 not in '>=3.10'

   1.11 is the last release that installs on 3.8.

3. requirements.txt asks for an unpinned `qiling`, which now resolves to 1.4.x.
   Pinned to 1.2.4, the last release contemporary with efi_fuzz.

4. Qiling renamed the constructor's `output` string argument to `verbose`,
   taking a QL_VERBOSE enum, before 1.2.4:

       TypeError: __init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'output'

   "trace" maps to QL_VERBOSE.DISASM and "default" to QL_VERBOSE.DEFAULT.
   The tests still use output=; they are left alone, since running them is a
   separate exercise from running the tool.

5. qiling 1.2.4 indexes x86 control registers that newer unicorn no longer
   exports, so an unpinned unicorn gives:

       NameError: name 'UC_X86_REG_CR5' is not defined

   Pinned to unicorn 1.0.3, which qiling 1.2.4 was built against.

diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
index 12f9232..8536504 100644
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -25,10 +25,10 @@ RUN wget https://github.com/JonathanSalwan/Triton/archive/v0.8.1.tar.gz \
 RUN git clone https://github.com/AFLplusplus/AFLplusplus.git && cd AFLplusplus/ && git checkout 2.68c && make \
     && cd unicorn_mode && ./build_unicorn_support.sh && cd .. && make install && cd /
 
-RUN wget https://bootstrap.pypa.io/get-pip.py && python3 get-pip.py
+RUN wget https://bootstrap.pypa.io/pip/3.8/get-pip.py && python3 get-pip.py
 
 COPY requirements.txt efi_fuzz_requirements.txt
 # uefi-firmware-parser in pypi is too old, let's use the one from github
-RUN pip3 install git+https://github.com/theopolis/uefi-firmware-parser.git 
+RUN pip3 install "uefi-firmware==1.11" 
 RUN pip3 install -r efi_fuzz_requirements.txt
 RUN pip3 install debugpy
